ssion of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Rosemary Tambouret MD Signed On  20 MAY 04 at 10 47 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast   is a 750 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm simple mastectomy specimen with a long stitch designating the 12 o clock aspect and a short stitch at the axilla measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm    There is an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 5 2cm irregular to oval tan white  blue stained portion of skin  No scar is identified  There is a centrally located REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm unremarkable nipple  The anterior aspect is inked blue  the posterior black  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal an unremarkable tan yellow to pink lobulated blue stained fibrofatty cut surface with no discrete masses or lesions identified  Within the minimum amount of attached stitched axilla  no lymph nodes are identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A  Representative sections of posterior margin  B  Representative section of skin and nipple  C J  Representative sections of fibrous tissue  K M  Representative sections of tissue from the stitched axilla  Z II  Additional tissue sections from mastectomy  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan yellow lymph node which is entirely submitted for frozen section as FX  1  and  1A  now as N and O  respectively  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary lymph nodes   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm unoriented tan yellow to pink lobulated portion of adipose tissue containing multiple tan pink rubbery lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 2 9cm in maximum dimension  The lymph nodes are entirely submitted as follows  P  One bisected lymph node  Q  Five whole lymph nodes  R  One bisected lymph node  S  One bisected lymph node  T  One bisected lymph node  U X  One whole lymph node  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast scar tissue   are two unoriented elongated portions of tan white unremarkable skin measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  Both portions are serially sectioned  and representative sections are submitted in cassette Y  Gross Description by  JENNIFER NASH Resident  RESIDENT FREE SERVICE  SGR      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1 AND  1A  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL   EXCISION  POSITIVE FOR CARCINOMA  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT  MASTECTOMY   SOME FIRM AREAS BUT NO DEFINITE CARCINOMA SEEN GROSSLY  O R  Resident  STEWART M  KNOEPP  MD   Ph D  O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL   EXCISION PART B  BREAST LEFT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART C  LYMPH NODE LEFT AXILLA  DISSECTION PART D  SCAR RIGHT BREAST  EXCISION , No.
