 the central part of the fibrotic area   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the anterior margin closest to the fibrotic area   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections of the unremarkable breast away from the previous resection   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cross section of nipple  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right breast   is a 17 x 16 x 3cm right simple mastectomy specimen oriented with a stitch designating 12 o clock  The anterior surface is remarkable for a REMOVED_DATE x 3cm skin ellipse including a nipple not 1cm in diameter  The nipple areolar complex is grossly unremarkable  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior   blue  posterior   black  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a large fibrous area  5 x 3 x 3cm in the lower outer aspect of the specimen  The rest of the specimen is grossly unremarkable  The area of fibrosis is grossly 2cm from the posterior resection margin and grossly abuts the anterior resection margin  Specimen is sectioned and submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Described fibrous area with the closest anterior and posterior resection margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the fibrotic area   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative sections of the breast parenchyma   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cross section of the nipple  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left breast skin   are 3 thin wormlike skin fragments  measuring in length 3cm  2cm and 1 5cm and  0 1cm in width each  entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right breast skin   is a 15cm long and 0 2cm in width skin ellipse  The specimen is entirely sectioned and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH 01   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 04 33 21PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making 