ds to the deep margin  Apart from the biopsy cavity  the remaining breast parenchyma is composed of yellow  soft  lobulated adipose tissue with interposed rubbery white fibrous tissue with several cysts  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 0cm in greatest dimension  Section Code  A  nipple B  skin with scar C  biopsy cavity with anterior soft tissue margin D  biopsy cavity with overlying skin E  fibrous area surrounding biopsy cavity with deep soft tissue margin F K  biopsy cavity  representative L M  fibrous breast parenchyma  representative  Labeled  axillary tissue   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  Sectioning reveals a 2 5cm in diameter  tan to fatty ovoid lymph node  Bisected and entirely submitted in N through O  Labeled  right central breast tissue  is a 145 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm aggregate of multiple pieces of breast parenchyma  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  One of the pieces contains an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm skin ellipse  The specimens are sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma  A representative section of skin with underlying breast tissue is submitted in P  Ten representative sections of breast parenchyma are submitted in Q through U  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Stamatina Kaptain  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT  PART B  AXILLARY TISSUE  LEFT  PART C  BREAST  RIGHT CENTRAL   TISSUE   report_end  , No.
